    "attributes": {
        "action": "Maintain current regulations to allow public firework use to continue ",
        "additional_details": "In our view, Parliament should be in support of this as without Nov 5th our politics could have been very different.\r\n \r\nThe UK has traditions and we believe those traditions should be upheld and not put into the hands of commercial businesses which hold licensed displays you have to pay for. We believe that every member of the public has the right to celebrate their traditions how they like.",
        "background": "We want the Government to allow members of the public to enjoy using fireworks without the fear of being branded a nuisance. November the 5th and New Year\u2019s Eve, as well as many other traditions, are celebrated with fireworks.",
